# Generated media is never committed: the spike generates it (cmd/genframes +
# ffmpeg) and the commands are in README.md.
results/media/
results/bin/
results/logs/

# Raw per-frame logs: ~1 MB per run, regenerated by tools/run-part-a.sh and
# re-analysable with cmd/analyze. The aggregated per-run reports and the
# verification log ARE committed as the evidence behind FINDINGS.md.
results/send-*.json
results/client-*.json
results/page-*.json

# Part B: the raw run log (~1 MB, one entry per encoded frame), the screenshots
# the strip was located in, and the driver's page dump. The analysed report and
# summary ARE committed, as the evidence behind FINDINGS.md.
results/live-*.json
results/clockprobe-*.json
results/diag/
